KNOWNBUG
main.cpp
--cpp11
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ copy constructor ran once: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ handler binds to the copy: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.3\] line \d+ WRONG \(must FAIL\): FAILURE$
^\*\* 1 of \d+ failed
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
--
remove_cpp_exceptions (set_inflight_exception) lowers a THROW to an
assignment of the operand to a per-throw-site static object, a bitwise copy:
the copy constructor never runs, so copies stays 0 and x.copied is false.
The exception object has to be initialized by the constructor that
copy-initialization selects ([dcl.init.general]/16.6.2).
